<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>{{ t("welcome.page.title", "Welcome — targum") }}</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{{ asset('words.css') }}{{ asset('arrival.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
<script>window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";</script>
</head>
{#- The arrival, on a page of its own (design.md §12, "Home is Your targums, and Continue
    leads it", 2026-10-08). It stood at the top of Learn; Learn is gone, and the FirstRun
    boards draw the questions as screens of their own, one a screen, before home. Home
    sends a new reader here (`home.js`), and `arrival.js` sends anybody it has nothing to
    ask straight back. -#}
<body class="words welcome">
{% set here = 'welcome' %}
{% set title = '' %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
<script>{{ asset('building.js') }}</script>

<main id="page">
  <section class="arrival" id="arrival" hidden aria-labelledby="arrival-asks">
    <div class="arrival-top">
      <p class="arrival-step" id="arrival-step"></p>
      {#- EN · RU, for a Russian reader whose browser did not say so: Latin letters, so a
          reader who does not read Russian sees none (design.md §12, 2026-09-28). Drawn
          by `learn.js` only while the language question is not asked. -#}
      <p class="arrival-switch" id="arrival-switch" hidden></p>
    </div>
    {#- Which language they read, before anything that has to be read (2026-09-20). Asked
        in every language it offers at once, each row in its own name, because a reader
        who cannot read "What are you interested in?" cannot be asked it. Drawn by
        `learn.js`, and only for somebody who has never said: an account the operator
        marked, a press on the front door's switcher and the conversation's own
        question are all answers already. -#}
    <div class="arrival-screen" id="arrival-language" hidden>
      <p class="arrival-asks" id="arrival-asks-language"></p>
      <div class="arrival-levels arrival-tongues" id="arrival-tongues" role="group" aria-labelledby="arrival-asks-language"></div>
    </div>
    {#- The welcome (David, 2026-09-28: "very weird to come and see this as first
        screen. No welcome, no telling you where you are, no asking your name, just a
        question"). Says where they are and what happens next, and asks what to call
        them — optional, and only where there is an account to keep it. Not a question
        the bars count. -#}
    <div class="arrival-screen" id="arrival-welcome" hidden>
      <p class="arrival-asks" id="arrival-asks-welcome">{{ t("learn.arrival.welcome", "Welcome to targum") }}</p>
      <p class="arrival-hint">{{ t("learn.arrival.welcome-what", "You learn Hebrew here from real texts and videos, with a translation beside every line and any word explained with a tap.") }}</p>
      <p class="arrival-hint">{{ t("learn.arrival.welcome-next", "A few quick questions first, then we’ll open something for you.") }}</p>
      <div class="arrival-name" id="arrival-name-row" hidden>
        <label for="arrival-name">{{ t("learn.arrival.what-to-call-you", "What should we call you?") }} <span class="arrival-optional">{{ t("learn.arrival.optional-word", "Optional") }}</span></label>
        <input id="arrival-name" type="text" autocomplete="given-name" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="arrival-screen" id="arrival-subjects">
      <p class="arrival-asks" id="arrival-asks">{{ t("learn.arrival.what-are-you-interested-in", "What are you interested in?") }}</p>
      <p class="arrival-hint">{{ t("learn.arrival.pick-three-or-more", "Pick three or more. We'll use them to choose texts for you.") }}</p>
      <div class="arrival-doors" id="arrival-doors" role="group" aria-labelledby="arrival-asks"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="arrival-screen" id="arrival-level" hidden>
      <p class="arrival-asks" id="arrival-asks-level">{{ t("learn.arrival.how-much-hebrew", "How much Hebrew do you know?") }}</p>
      <p class="arrival-hint">{{ t("learn.arrival.level-hint", "You’ll start there, and we’ll adjust as you mark words.") }}</p>
      <div class="arrival-levels" id="arrival-levels" role="group" aria-labelledby="arrival-asks-level"></div>
    </div>
    {#- The way into Claude and ChatGPT, last, and only to a signed-in reader with no
        connection while the connector is open (design.md §12, "The connector is met on
        the way in"). It tells rather than asks: the address and Copy, every app's steps
        in a new tab, and Open for the text the answers chose. Filled by `learn.js`. -#}
    <div class="arrival-screen" id="arrival-connect" hidden>
      <p class="arrival-optional arrival-optional-lead">{{ t("learn.arrival.optional-word", "Optional") }}</p>
      <p class="arrival-asks" id="arrival-asks-connect">{{ t("learn.arrival.connect-asks", "Use targum in Claude or ChatGPT") }}</p>
      <p class="arrival-hint">{{ t("learn.arrival.connect-hint", "You don’t need this to use targum. If you use Claude or ChatGPT, you can add targum there and practise Hebrew with the words you know. You can do it later.") }}</p>
      <div class="arrival-connect-steps" id="arrival-connect-steps"></div>
      <p class="arrival-connect-more"><a href="/connect#install" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t("learn.arrival.connect-every-app", "Learn more") }}</a></p>
    </div>
    <p class="arrival-foot">
      {#- The way back from the second question to the first (2026-09-20). A reader who
          pressed Next a subject early, or wants to see what they chose, had no way to:
          the arrival went one way. Drawn on the second screen only, and a ghost like
          Skip — going back is not an answer. -#}
      <button type="button" class="arrival-skip arrival-back" id="arrival-back" hidden>{{ t("learn.arrival.back", "Back") }}</button>
      <button type="button" class="arrival-done" id="arrival-done" disabled>{{ t("learn.arrival.next", "Next") }}</button>
      <button type="button" class="arrival-skip" id="arrival-skip">{{ t("learn.arrival.skip", "Skip") }}</button>
      <span class="arrival-count" id="arrival-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </p>
  </section>
  <p class="arrival-waiting" id="arrival-waiting" role="status">{{ t("welcome.page.opening", "Opening…") }}</p>
</main>

{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}

<script>
window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";
window.TARGUM_INTO = {{ into|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in languages %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };
window.TARGUM_CONNECTOR = {{ connector|tojson }};
{% if strings %}window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};
{% endif %}</script>
<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('charts.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lang.js') }}</script>
{#- What was pressed on the way in (targum-internal#127): a `control` event carries a name
    and the window's width, never which text. Silent signed out and where turned off. -#}
<script>{{ asset('events.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('sync.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('account.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('covers.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('shelf.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('scenes.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('arrival.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
